00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.390
let the rich guy pay for
damage you don't intend to fix.

260
00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.890
Just give the man some money

261
00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:47.230
so we can leave.

262
00:12:52.761 --> 00:12:54.231
Congratulations!

263
00:13:02.252 --> 00:13:03.991
- He was there.
- I think Tuxhorn was in the car.

264
00:13:04.031 --> 00:13:06.091
- So did we get it or not?
- Nope.

265
00:13:06.131 --> 00:13:07.431
Nothing.

266
00:13:19.813 --> 00:13:22.062
Can I help you?

267
00:13:23.762 --> 00:13:25.632
So how did you find me?

268
00:13:25.662 --> 00:13:27.292
I never lost you.

269
00:13:27.332 --> 00:13:29.892
The. uh. the new nose
threw me a bit. but--

270
00:13:29.932 --> 00:13:31.662
What do you want. Don?

271
00:13:31.692 --> 00:13:33.062
I got customers.

272
00:13:33.092 --> 00:13:36.205
Look. back in the days. when
you worked with the Company...

273
00:13:36.206 --> 00:13:37.362
Well. for the Company.

274
00:13:37.392 --> 00:13:38.862
I did economic forecasts
of their operations.

275
00:13:38.892 --> 00:13:40.632
I mean. I wasn't one of the guys--

276
00:13:40.662 --> 00:13:41.633
But you had access.

277
00:13:41.663 --> 00:13:43.263
Come on.
the last time I helped you.

278
00:13:43.293 --> 00:13:44.733
the only thing I got out of it

279
00:13:44.763 --> 00:13:47.093
was plastic surgery
and a $100.000 pay cut.

280
00:13:47.133 --> 00:13:49.532
You know. so either you buy
one of these exceptional family cars.

281
00:13:49.567 --> 00:13:52.098
with above average gas mileage.
or you leave me the hell alone.

282
00:13:52.833 --> 00:13:54.133
I know about Scylla.

283
00:13:56.533 --> 00:13:58.093
And I'm going after it.

284
00:13:59.293 --> 00:14:01.393
You know. I knew you were crazy.

285
00:14:01.433 --> 00:14:02.863
I didn't know you were stupid. too.

286
00:14:02.893 --> 00:14:05.533
Well. let's just say I was
able to get hands on it.

287
00:14:05.563 --> 00:14:07.464
It's my understanding that
Scylla could only be used

288
00:14:07.494 --> 00:14:09.364
if it's plugged into a decoder box

289
00:14:09.394 --> 00:14:11.714
that's hidden in one of the
Company facilities. Am I right?

290
00:14:12.064 --> 00:14:14.110
You know. I wish I could help.
but I can't.

291
00:14:14.934 --> 00:14:16.234
No. you are helping. Jasper.

292
00:14:16.264 --> 00:14:18.834
Just a matter of whether
you do it before or after

293
00:14:18.864 --> 00:14:20.894
I shame you in front
of your co-workers here.

294
00:14:26.394 --> 00:14:28.194
Tell me where the Company
keeps the box. Jasper.

295
00:14:28.234 --> 00:14:29.264
Could be anywhere.
I don't know.

296
00:14:29.294 --> 00:14:30.794
Somebody does.

297
00:14:30.834 --> 00:14:31.795
Right?

298
00:14:31.835 --> 00:14:33.935
Somebody that you might
have access to.

299
00:14:33.965 --> 00:14:35.335
You know. if you go down this road.

300
00:14:35.365 --> 00:14:37.135
your government job
won't protect you.

301
00:14:37.165 --> 00:14:39.895
Then I better not
get caught. right?

302
00:14:39.935 --> 00:14:42.595
If I don't find something to eat soon.

303
00:14:42.635 --> 00:14:44.735
I don't know what I'm gonna do.

304
00:14:44.765 --> 00:14:46.035
I'm not gonna make it.

305
00:14:46.495 --> 00:14:49.135
We just got to keep...
got to keep talking. Sancho.

306
00:14:49.165 --> 00:14:51.595
Keep our brains focused
on something other than

307
00:14:51.635 --> 00:14:54.665
our empty bellies and
our dry mouths. okay?

308
00:14:54.695 --> 00:14:55.935
Come on!

309
00:14:55.965 --> 00:14:58.836
Let's start with. uh.
your-your favorite color.

310
00:15:04.796 --> 00:15:06.836
Aah. hell you doing?!

311
00:15:08.066 --> 00:15:09.196
I'm hungry. Teddy.

312
00:15:09.236 --> 00:15:11.316
Why should the both of us die
out here when one of us

313
00:15:11.696 --> 00:15:13.017
could help the other one survive?

314
00:15:13.036 --> 00:15:15.496
You don't want to do this. Please!

315
00:15:15.536 --> 00:15:17.696
I'll make it quick. I promise!

316
00:15:21.366 --> 00:15:23.737
Sancho?

317
00:15:28.797 --> 00:15:30.567
Sancho!

318
00:15:30.597 --> 00:15:34.867
Why'd you have to go
and do something so...

319
00:16:11.839 --> 00:16:13.839
so Tuxhorn doesn't have
the card on him.

320
00:16:13.869 --> 00:16:15.099
It gotta be in there. right?

321
00:16:18.499 --> 00:16:21.289
Look. there's no way we're getting
on that house without being seen.

322
00:16:21.439 --> 00:16:22.839
I know.

323
00:16:22.869 --> 00:16:25.069
Well. if the card's in
there. how are we gonna copy it?

324
00:16:25.099 --> 00:16:26.039
We're not.

325
00:16:26.069 --> 00:16:28.969
She's gonna do it for us.

326
00:16:44.253 --> 00:16:46.400
What you reading?

327
00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.340
"There is no fighting her.

328
00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:50.070
"No power can fight her.

329
00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:53.200
"All that avails is flight."

330
00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.000
That's Homer.

331
00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:56.300
That's from The Odyssey.

332
00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:58.300
- Is this from my father's folder?
- Yeah.

333
00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:00.540
And it explains why
Scylla sounded so familiar.

334
00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:03.541
If I'm not mistaken. it's
from that chapter in the book

335
00:17:03.571 --> 00:17:06.518
where Odysseus is told
he has to confront a monster...

336
00:17:06.801 --> 00:17:09.271
...known as Scylla.

337
00:17:09.301 --> 00:17:11.441
Wonder why he wrote this down.

338
00:17:11.471 --> 00:17:13.271
I could be wrong.
but I believe

339
00:17:13.301 --> 00:17:15.841
Odysseus is told that in order to

340
00:17:15.871 --> 00:17:18.001
continue on his path.
to pass Scylla.

341
00:17:18.041 --> 00:17:21.001
it'll require the
sacrifice of six of his men.

342
00:17:21.041 --> 00:17:23.941
His only other alternative
is to abandon his path

343
00:17:23.971 --> 00:17:27.642
and he chooses to
make the sacrifice.

344
00:17:27.672 --> 00:17:31.172
Well. it's a hell of a choice.

345
00:17:34.102 --> 00:17:35.779
One I'm not sure I'm
comfortable making.

346
00:17:39.702 --> 00:17:44.272
Sara. um. about tomorrow.
the plan.

347
00:17:44.273 --> 00:17:45.273
housekeeper...

348
00:17:47.072 --> 00:17:48.372
If you're not up to it--

349
00:17:48.402 --> 00:17:50.442
No. no. I am.

350
00:18:01.887 --> 00:18:06.565
Tell me. is Claudia
Mauricio a good roommate?

351
00:18:14.173 --> 00:18:16.273
A good person?

352
00:18:19.635 --> 00:18:22.404
I hope she feels the same about you.

353
00:18:27.944 --> 00:18:30.984
Oh. Shelby. you wouldn't believe
the traffic on the...

354
00:18:32.274 --> 00:18:34.804
You'll want to be quiet now.

355
00:18:34.844 --> 00:18:36.474
Claudia.

356
00:18:36.504 --> 00:18:39.700
There are levels of clearance
at the Department of Corrections

357
00:18:39.701 --> 00:18:43.780
that are simply not available.
even for friends as connected as mine.

358
00:18:44.275 --> 00:18:47.275
So. listen carefully.

359
00:18:47.305 --> 00:18:51.645
If you even remotely
value your friend's life.

360
00:18:53.045 --> 00:18:55.775
You're going to use your
security code to access

361
00:18:55.805 --> 00:18:58.075
the records for prisoner transfers.

362
00:18:58.105 --> 00:19:00.996
And tell me where they
sent Michael Scofield

363
00:19:01.445 --> 00:19:02.845
and Lincoln Burrows.

364
00:19:33.285 --> 00:19:33.997
Can I take that for you?

365
00:19:34.207 --> 00:19:36.147
Thanks! Sure.

366
00:19:39.577 --> 00:19:41.207
That's a great bag.

367
00:19:41.247 --> 00:19:42.547
Can I ask you where you got it?

368
00:19:42.577 --> 00:19:44.453
It was a gift from my boss.
so I don't really know.

369
00:19:44.488 --> 00:19:45.707
Sorry.

370
00:19:45.747 --> 00:19:47.347
- Sure.
- Thanks!

371
00:19:47.377 --> 00:19:48.407
There you go.

372
00:19:48.447 --> 00:19:50.707
I. uh... I can never find a good bag.

373
00:19:50.747 --> 00:19:53.307
I'm a teacher.
and I have books

374
00:19:53.347 --> 00:19:54.941
and grading materials and...

375
00:19:54.942 --> 00:19:58.188
I should probably go ahead and just
invest in a wagon one of these days.

376
00:19:59.208 --> 00:20:01.278
Yeah. that's why I love this bag.

377
00:20:01.308 --> 00:20:03.308
It has so many pockets.

378
00:20:03.348 --> 00:20:04.978
Do you mind if I take a look?

379
00:20:05.008 --> 00:20:06.308
Oh. no.

380
00:20:06.348 --> 00:20:07.808
Thanks.

381
00:20:27.809 --> 00:20:31.049
Oh. thank God. thank God!

382
00:20:32.009 --> 00:20:33.549
You all right. mister?

383
00:20:33.579 --> 00:20:36.949
Yeah. my damn truck blew
a gasket a few miles back.

384
00:20:36.979 --> 00:20:39.209
I've been. uh. hoofing it ever since.

385
00:20:39.249 --> 00:20:40.449
Where you headed?

386
00:20:40.479 --> 00:20:42.579
San Diego.

387
00:20:42.609 --> 00:20:45.349
Hell. we can give you
a ride. if you'd like.

388
00:20:46.549 --> 00:20:47.886
Hey. what's wrong. man?

389
00:20:47.887 --> 00:20:49.180
Eat some bad Mexican?

390
00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:53.180
Something like that.

391
00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:00.380
Same as yesterday.
right on schedule.

392
00:21:06.955 --> 00:21:08.516
She better have that
thing in her purse.

393
00:21:15.851 --> 00:21:17.051
Tuxhorn Residence.

394
00:21:17.081 --> 00:21:18.611
Hello. I'm from the alarm company.

395
00:21:18.651 --> 00:21:22.565
We've been receiving some. uh.
strange signals from your property.

396
00:21:22.581 --> 00:21:24.311
We'd like you to check
the windows. please.

397
00:21:24.351 --> 00:21:26.851
Make sure all the
contacts are still active.

398
00:21:26.881 --> 00:21:28.051
All the windows?

399
00:21:28.081 --> 00:21:29.381
Yes. ma'am.

400
00:21:29.411 --> 00:21:30.781
Every room in the house.

401
00:21:33.251 --> 00:21:34.981
Okay. hold on.

402
00:21:39.612 --> 00:21:41.412
Does she still have the bag?

403
00:21:41.452 --> 00:21:42.712
Yeah.

404
00:21:47.852 --> 00:21:49.182
She's got it.

405
00:21:49.212 --> 00:21:51.612
I'm picking up all kinds
of gak from the house. man.

406
00:21:51.652 --> 00:21:54.212
Small stuff. maybe a digital
camera. an MP3 player.

407
00:21:54.252 --> 00:21:56.152
Nothing of the size of what
we're looking for. though.

408
00:21:56.182 --> 00:21:57.252
Keep her moving.

409
00:21:57.282 --> 00:21:58.382
So far. so good. ma'am.

410
00:21:58.412 --> 00:22:00.612
Uh. please move on
to the next room.

411
00:22:04.583 --> 00:22:06.683
How we doing?

412
00:22:06.713 --> 00:22:07.983
Still don't got it.

413
00:22:11.413 --> 00:22:15.187
If the card's in there.
it'd be in some kind of a... safe. office.

414
00:22:15.513 --> 00:22:16.634
Ma'am. our system is showing

415
00:22:16.653 --> 00:22:18.913
that the malfunction
is coming from a room

416
00:22:18.953 --> 00:22:21.953
that's designated as.
uh. an office or a den.

417
00:22:21.983 --> 00:22:23.083
You mean the library?

418
00:22:23.113 --> 00:22:24.753
Mister doesn't like me going in there.

419
00:22:24.783 --> 00:22:26.577
Well. I think he'd like it
even less if you went home

420
00:22:26.679 --> 00:22:29.284
without properly setting the
alarm first. don't you think?

421
00:22:30.814 --> 00:22:32.914
All right. I'll check.

422
00:22:37.654 --> 00:22:38.684
We got something.

423
00:22:38.714 --> 00:22:39.714
The card?

424
00:22:39.754 --> 00:22:40.954
Oh. yeah!

425
00:22:40.984 --> 00:22:42.354
File's so big it can't be anything else.

426
00:22:42.384 --> 00:22:43.611
Now you just gotta keep her there

427
00:22:43.646 --> 00:22:45.084
for two minutes while
it finishes the burn.

428
00:22:45.114 --> 00:22:46.784
Stall her. we need two minutes.

429
00:22:46.814 --> 00:22:48.054
Ma'am. I think we found
the source of our problem.

430
00:22:48.084 --> 00:22:49.654
If you could just stay
at that particular window

431
00:22:49.684 --> 00:22:53.428
and hold it closed while we reset
the system. that should do it.

432
00:23:04.115 --> 00:23:05.285
Talk to me. Roland.

433
00:23:05.315 --> 00:23:07.085
It's almost there.
almost. almost.

434
00:23:07.115 --> 00:23:08.985
Come on. come on.
come on. come on.

435
00:23:15.855 --> 00:23:17.155
Come on.

436
00:23:22.416 --> 00:23:24.156
- Got it!
- Got it.

437
00:23:24.186 --> 00:23:26.686
All right. ma'am. thank
you so much for your help.

438
00:23:33.116 --> 00:23:36.016
All we need to do
now. man. is just...

439
00:23:36.056 --> 00:23:39.156
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.
she's heading back inside.

440
00:23:39.186 --> 00:23:40.916
- What for?
- I don't know.

441
00:23:44.817 --> 00:23:46.257
Oh. no.

442
00:23:46.287 --> 00:23:47.417
No. we're good.

443
00:23:48.287 --> 00:23:49.887
She's out.

444
00:24:04.957 --> 00:24:06.087
Hey! Oh!

445
00:24:06.117 --> 00:24:07.687
Hey. stop it!

446
00:24:07.717 --> 00:24:09.087
Just wait here.

447
00:24:16.558 --> 00:24:18.418
I actually had to slow down
not to catch you.

448
00:24:18.458 --> 00:24:20.558
I think I pulled a groin.

449
00:24:23.218 --> 00:24:24.588
It's not in the bag.

450
00:24:27.501 --> 00:24:29.288
- It's not here.
- How could it not be in here?

451
00:24:29.318 --> 00:24:32.158
The device. it's not here.
Give me it!

452
00:24:33.888 --> 00:24:35.789
Son of a bitch!

453
00:24:40.389 --> 00:24:44.219
Twenty-six. twenty-seven.
twenty-eight...

454
00:25:08.990 --> 00:25:10.120
Go ahead.

455
00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:13.411
Before Burrows and Scofield
were allegedlly transferred

456
00:25:13.412 --> 00:25:16.120
to Arlington. someone posted their bail.

457
00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:17.660
I need to know who.

458
00:25:17.690 --> 00:25:19.160
I'm showing a Bruce Bennett.

459
00:25:19.190 --> 00:25:21.690
former aid to Governor
Frank Tancredi.

460
00:25:37.621 --> 00:25:38.991
You think it fell out?

461
00:25:39.021 --> 00:25:40.291
We looked everywhere.

462
00:25:40.321 --> 00:25:42.021
You think we got the thing copied?

463
00:25:42.061 --> 00:25:44.391
Like I said. I can't read the content

464
00:25:44.421 --> 00:25:46.491
without downloading the device. but...

465
00:25:46.521 --> 00:25:48.621
unless this Tuxhorn's got.
like. a 50.000-hour TiVo.

466
00:25:48.661 --> 00:25:49.921
then. yeah. I think we got it.

467
00:25:49.961 --> 00:25:51.692
Doesn't matter if we got it
if we can't find it.

468
00:25:51.722 --> 00:25:52.562
Where the hell is it?

469
00:25:54.422 --> 00:25:56.122
It's still inside the house.

470
00:25:57.392 --> 00:25:58.562
That's why the maid went back inside.

471
00:25:58.592 --> 00:26:00.793
She must have found it.
assumed it belonged to her boss.

472
00:26:00.962 --> 00:26:02.192
and then she left it behind.

473
00:26:02.222 --> 00:26:03.892
Well. then guess what.
fellas. it's game over.

474
00:26:03.922 --> 00:26:06.442
You know how many months it took
me to make that thing. Michael?

475
00:26:06.562 --> 00:26:08.062
What. you just think I
can whip up another one

476
00:26:08.092 --> 00:26:10.262
- in a couple of seconds?
- Losing it is not the problem.

477
00:26:10.292 --> 00:26:12.162
If they find it. that's the problem.

478
00:26:12.192 --> 00:26:15.162
If they find out someone was
after that card. we're done.

479
00:26:15.193 --> 00:26:17.593
What do you mean. done?
What does that mean?

480
00:26:17.623 --> 00:26:18.893
Does that mean we're
gonna go back to prison?

481
00:26:18.923 --> 00:26:19.963
Are they gonna kill us?

482
00:26:19.993 --> 00:26:21.823
- What the hell does that mean?
- Shut up!

483
00:26:24.123 --> 00:26:25.623
Means we're going in to get it.

484
00:26:33.223 --> 00:26:34.323
If we had a few days.
we could figure out

485
00:26:34.393 --> 00:26:37.293
a way to pull this off. but I gather
we don't have that kind of time.

486
00:26:37.323 --> 00:26:38.793
Yeah. you gather right.

487
00:26:38.823 --> 00:26:42.111
Look. if you want us to get that device
out of there. you gotta throw us a bone.

488
00:26:42.564 --> 00:26:43.324
give us some extra help.

489
00:26:43.364 --> 00:26:45.963
What you're asking for requires
involving additional people.

490
00:26:45.964 --> 00:26:47.724
which. given the covert
nature of this operation.

491
00:26:47.764 --> 00:26:48.824
I cannot do.

492
00:26:48.864 --> 00:26:50.124
Then you're asking for the impossible.

493
00:26:50.164 --> 00:26:51.794
No. what I'm asking
for is competence. okay?

494
00:26:51.824 --> 00:26:53.664
I'm not the one who
put the entire mission

495
00:26:53.694 --> 00:26:55.294
in the hands of a damn maid.

496
00:26:59.024 --> 00:27:01.864
Look. if the Company finds that
copy of Scylla before we do.

497
00:27:01.894 --> 00:27:04.024
that's it. Michael. that's ball game.

498
00:27:04.064 --> 00:27:05.565
They're gonna find
out who was behind it.

499
00:27:05.595 --> 00:27:06.625
and they're going to ghost us.

500
00:27:06.665 --> 00:27:07.765
All of us.

501
00:27:08.539 --> 00:27:09.495
Are you okay?

502
00:27:11.125 --> 00:27:13.465
Yeah.

503
00:27:14.395 --> 00:27:16.365
I'm fine.

504
00:27:17.525 --> 00:27:19.993
Look. I didn't choose you to do this
because I had you in custody.

505
00:27:20.095 --> 00:27:22.731
I chose you to do this because
I believed you could pull it off.

506
00:27:22.732 --> 00:27:26.598
Yeah. well. a lot of people have believed
in me in the last few months. Agent Self.

507
00:27:27.325 --> 00:27:30.025
Not all of them are alive today.

508
00:27:32.196 --> 00:27:35.196
Can you get me back the device or not?

509
00:27:39.796 --> 00:27:41.126
All right. this is what we got.

510
00:27:41.166 --> 00:27:43.726
The housekeeper saw the device
as she was leaving the house.

511
00:27:43.766 --> 00:27:46.596
Then she disappears back
inside for 15 seconds.

512
00:27:46.626 --> 00:27:47.626
So. we know. wherever it is.

513
00:27:47.666 --> 00:27:48.826
it's somewhere close to the door.

514
00:27:48.866 --> 00:27:50.126
So. 15 seconds.

515
00:27:50.166 --> 00:27:51.996
that's all we gotta buy ourselves.

516
00:27:52.026 --> 00:27:56.031
Listen. I'm not sure how close we're gonna
get to this house. let alone inside of it.

517
00:27:56.267 --> 00:27:57.507
but let's-let's say that we do.

518
00:27:57.527 --> 00:27:59.688
The alarm they got installed
in this house is triggered

519
00:28:00.427 --> 00:28:03.267
1.2 seconds after broken
contact in any door or window.

520
00:28:03.297 --> 00:28:05.727
Which would immediately send
the private security guards

521
00:28:05.767 --> 00:28:07.927
with their 47 guns
rushing into the property.

522
00:28:07.967 --> 00:28:09.567
And after 30 seconds. the alarm company

523
00:28:09.597 --> 00:28:10.867
will dispatch vehicles to the property.

524
00:28:10.897 --> 00:28:12.397
Three to four. depending
on availability.

525
00:28:12.427 --> 00:28:16.124
After confirmation of a break-in.
they'll dispatch additional vehicles

526
00:28:16.125 --> 00:28:18.427
to seal off any and all
exits from the property.

527
00:28:18.467 --> 00:28:19.427
I don't know about this. Michael.

528
00:28:19.467 --> 00:28:22.483
It's getting pretty clear why they
hired a bunch of cons to do this job.

529
00:28:22.568 --> 00:28:24.668
It's not because they
wanted it off the books.

530
00:28:24.698 --> 00:28:25.928
It's because we're expendable.

531
00:28:25.968 --> 00:28:29.368
Who's gonna care if a bunch
of crooks wind up dead?

532
00:28:29.398 --> 00:28:30.398
It's suicide.

533
00:28:30.428 --> 00:28:32.269
I'm gonna keep looking
and see what I can find.

534
00:28:37.768 --> 00:28:39.528
That quote from The Odyssey.

535
00:28:39.568 --> 00:28:40.828
What about it?

536
00:28:40.868 --> 00:28:44.068
I just. I can't shake that line.

537
00:28:44.098 --> 00:28:46.229
"All that avails is flight."

538
00:28:47.769 --> 00:28:50.669
What if flight is our only option. Linc?

539
00:28:52.069 --> 00:28:54.369
What if our father after
everything he discovered

540
00:28:54.370 --> 00:28:55.869
about the Company.
what...

541
00:28:57.429 --> 00:28:59.299
...what if that's what
he finally realized?

542
00:28:59.329 --> 00:29:01.629
You know. uh. the one
thing I remember most

543
00:29:01.669 --> 00:29:03.799
about Dad was the
back of his head.

544
00:29:03.829 --> 00:29:05.769
Always walk out the front door.

545
00:29:05.799 --> 00:29:08.069
Always running from something.

546
00:29:08.099 --> 00:29:10.469
Mom. us. himself.

547
00:29:10.499 --> 00:29:13.170
But the one thing he
never ran away from

548
00:29:13.200 --> 00:29:16.130
was his belief that the
Company needed to be taken down.

549
00:29:16.170 --> 00:29:18.370
And we got an opportunity to do that.

550
00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:20.630
Then this is our fight. not theirs.

551
00:29:20.670 --> 00:29:23.700
Man. this... this ain't Fox River.

552
00:29:23.730 --> 00:29:26.370
These guys chose to be here.

553
00:29:26.400 --> 00:29:28.700
Remember that.

554
00:29:28.730 --> 00:29:29.931
They got a choice.

555
00:31:11.203 --> 00:31:12.503
Almost...

556
00:31:12.504 --> 00:31:14.304
Ready?

557
00:31:17.275 --> 00:31:18.605
Go!

558
00:31:35.905 --> 00:31:38.106
- Let's go! Let's go! Go!
- The side-doors are locked...

559
00:31:38.505 --> 00:31:41.605
Go!

560
00:31:48.706 --> 00:31:49.906
- Come on.
- Let's go!

561
00:31:54.406 --> 00:31:55.876
Where's it coming from?

562
00:31:55.906 --> 00:31:57.106
It's across the street.

563
00:32:02.836 --> 00:32:05.806
Come on.

564
00:32:16.907 --> 00:32:18.977
Go.

565
00:32:29.107 --> 00:32:31.437
Just something across the street.

566
00:32:31.477 --> 00:32:33.138
We got a team checking it out now.

567
00:32:33.178 --> 00:32:35.908
You can get back inside. sir.

568
00:32:46.963 --> 00:32:48.438
That must be out of town.

569
00:32:52.939 --> 00:32:53.778
Yes!

570
00:32:56.378 --> 00:32:58.139
Daddy. is everything okay?

571
00:33:08.209 --> 00:33:09.879
Alex...

572
00:33:11.339 --> 00:33:13.539
Thanks. Jim!

573
00:33:13.579 --> 00:33:15.239
Alex!

574
00:33:15.279 --> 00:33:17.009
Let's go!

575
00:33:47.788 --> 00:33:48.581
Go!

576
00:33:59.481 --> 00:34:01.641
Don't turn around...

577
00:34:01.681 --> 00:34:04.841
unless you'd like to
experience a great deal of pain

578
00:34:04.881 --> 00:34:07.081
over an even greater length of time.

579
00:34:07.111 --> 00:34:10.181
You-you know. just-just
take whatever you want here.

580
00:34:10.211 --> 00:34:11.681
The only thing I want from you.

581
00:34:11.711 --> 00:34:15.982
Bruce. is the answer
to a simple question:

582
00:34:16.012 --> 00:34:18.582
Where are Michael Scofield
and Lincoln Burrows?

583
00:34:18.612 --> 00:34:20.682
I only know what-what I
read in the papers and--

584
00:34:20.712 --> 00:34:25.118
Three days ago. there were a
105 inmates in the Supermax wing

585
00:34:25.682 --> 00:34:29.012
of the U.S. penitentiary
in Livingston. Texas.

586
00:34:29.042 --> 00:34:31.842
where the brothers were allegedly sent.

587
00:34:31.882 --> 00:34:37.403
There are still 105 inmates there and no
one has been released during that time.

588
00:34:37.982 --> 00:34:40.840
Someone is playing a shell game. Bruce.

589
00:34:41.913 --> 00:34:45.383
I'm just trying to find out who.

590
00:34:45.413 --> 00:34:47.613
I have no criminal jurisdiction over...

591
00:34:47.643 --> 00:34:49.115
I know you bailed them out.

592
00:34:50.243 --> 00:34:52.715
I know you've been in
contact with Sara Tancredi.

593
00:34:53.113 --> 00:34:56.225
I swear to you. I-I have
no idea where they are.

594
00:34:59.183 --> 00:35:00.783
I guess we'll see about that.

595
00:35:07.714 --> 00:35:09.344
Good luck. Teddy!

596
00:35:09.384 --> 00:35:12.414
Who needs luck when you got
friends like you fellas. huh?

597
00:35:15.084 --> 00:35:17.893
Hey. you mind if I take this
old newspaper of yours with me?

598
00:35:17.894 --> 00:35:18.644
No problem.

599
00:35:18.684 --> 00:35:20.314
Sorry to hear about your friend. dude.

600
00:35:20.344 --> 00:35:22.368
Ahh. it's all right.

601
00:35:24.114 --> 00:35:25.614
He had a full life.

602
00:35:26.544 --> 00:35:27.714
Later. Teddy.

603
00:35:43.745 --> 00:35:45.845
There you go.

604
00:36:03.246 --> 00:36:04.516
Thirty-six.

605
00:36:05.476 --> 00:36:06.686
twenty-four.

606
00:36:06.716 --> 00:36:10.086
thirty-six.

607
00:36:52.996 --> 00:36:55.018
Did you get it?

608
00:36:55.048 --> 00:36:56.888
Let's make sure we got
what we wanted.

609
00:36:59.818 --> 00:37:01.348
- Linc.
- Yeah.

610
00:37:01.388 --> 00:37:03.148
Don't let that thing out of your sight.

611
00:37:03.188 --> 00:37:04.848
All right.

612
00:37:06.818 --> 00:37:07.748
We're halfway there.

613
00:37:07.788 --> 00:37:09.512
All we got to do is
that little B and E. and...

614
00:37:09.559 --> 00:37:11.019
we're out of here.

615
00:37:11.049 --> 00:37:13.019
Reminds me. I need to get ahold of Self.

616
00:37:13.049 --> 00:37:14.219
see when we can get started.

617
00:37:14.249 --> 00:37:16.749
So what are you gonna do
when all this is over?

618
00:37:19.049 --> 00:37:20.725
That's a good question.

619
00:37:24.112 --> 00:37:26.913
Brother. whatever this Scylla thing is.
it is a monster of a code.

620
00:37:46.920 --> 00:37:51.405
Sara. I was gonna come down here
and ask if you wanted to talk some more

621
00:37:51.650 --> 00:37:54.050
about what happened in Panama.

622
00:37:55.306 --> 00:37:57.426
but. um. I think I already
know what you're gonna say.

623
00:37:57.475 --> 00:37:59.591
How's that?

624
00:37:59.621 --> 00:38:02.691
Because you're a little like me.

625
00:38:02.721 --> 00:38:06.251
Because you're gonna say you're
fine. that you can handle it.

626
00:38:07.221 --> 00:38:08.851
So. umm...

627
00:38:08.891 --> 00:38:11.521
I'll just leave it at this.

628
00:38:11.551 --> 00:38:14.421
I'm here.

629
00:38:14.451 --> 00:38:16.321
Whenever you want to talk...

630
00:38:16.351 --> 00:38:17.491
I'm here.

631
00:38:19.421 --> 00:38:21.021
Thank you!

632
00:38:26.392 --> 00:38:29.392
You know that the only
thing that kept me alive

633
00:38:29.422 --> 00:38:32.492
when I was being held was
the thought of being with you.

634
00:38:34.792 --> 00:38:36.922
But I also knew that if
anything happened to me.

635
00:38:36.952 --> 00:38:38.622
you were gonna blame yourself. and
you would spend the rest of your life

636
00:38:38.652 --> 00:38:40.492
punishing yourself for it. and...

637
00:38:40.522 --> 00:38:43.192
I can't...

638
00:38:43.222 --> 00:38:44.692
bear the thought of that.

639
00:38:48.952 --> 00:38:52.053
So can we make a deal
right now that we're even.

640
00:38:52.093 --> 00:38:54.153
and just wipe the slate clean

641
00:38:54.193 --> 00:38:57.853
and no guilt and no responsibility?

642
00:38:57.893 --> 00:38:59.353
If we're gonna be together.

643
00:38:59.393 --> 00:39:01.653
I don't want it to be out
of a sense of obligation.

644
00:39:01.693 --> 00:39:06.972
Or-or even that we should be.
because of what we've been through.

645
00:39:07.123 --> 00:39:11.023
I-I... I just want to start over.

646
00:39:11.923 --> 00:39:13.853
Start over.

647
00:39:13.893 --> 00:39:15.754
Okay.

648
00:39:15.794 --> 00:39:20.054
But. uh. does that mean
I have to divorce my wife?

649
00:39:22.054 --> 00:39:24.550
Because you're still married
to a Russian stripper.

650
00:39:25.224 --> 00:39:27.094
Well. "A": I've been a little busy.

651
00:39:27.124 --> 00:39:30.094
and "B": I'm pretty sure she was Czech.

652
00:39:30.124 --> 00:39:32.024
Hey. Michael.

653
00:39:33.194 --> 00:39:34.254
What's wrong?

654
00:39:34.294 --> 00:39:36.094
Whatever it is. it ain't it.

655
00:39:36.124 --> 00:39:38.761
I don't understand. I thought
you said we copied the card.

656
00:39:38.994 --> 00:39:40.025
No. we did.

657
00:39:40.055 --> 00:39:41.625
But according to the encryption code...

658
00:39:41.655 --> 00:39:43.795
Okay. how do I make this clear?

659
00:39:43.825 --> 00:39:47.895
If-If Scylla was like a
pizza. all we got's a slice.

660
00:39:47.925 --> 00:39:49.995
So where's the rest of the data?

661
00:39:50.025 --> 00:39:51.295
I don't know.
I don't know.

662
00:39:51.325 --> 00:39:52.395
I mean...

663
00:39:52.425 --> 00:39:54.425
I mean. I don't know how
we didn't see this coming.

664
00:39:54.555 --> 00:39:56.095
I mean. it-it-it makes perfect sense.

665
00:39:56.125 --> 00:39:57.825
It's like the nuclear launch codes.

666
00:39:57.855 --> 00:40:00.016
You don't give all that
information to just one person.

667
00:40:00.025 --> 00:40:01.495
How many do you give it to?

668
00:40:01.525 --> 00:40:03.225
Okay. that quote your father held onto

669
00:40:03.255 --> 00:40:05.726
in The Odyssey. Scylla
is a six-headed monster

670
00:40:05.756 --> 00:40:07.526
that requires a
sacrifice of six soldiers

671
00:40:07.556 --> 00:40:08.656
in order to pass.

672
00:40:08.696 --> 00:40:11.426
So Scylla isn't one card.

673
00:40:12.565 --> 00:40:13.726
it's six.

674
00:40:20.856 --> 00:40:22.826
What does that mean?
How we gonna find

675
00:40:22.856 --> 00:40:23.826
five more of these things?

676
00:40:23.856 --> 00:40:25.996
Michael! Michael!

677
00:40:34.520 --> 00:40:35.227
I'm busy.

678
00:40:35.257 --> 00:40:37.697
I don't care what she looks like.

679
00:40:37.727 --> 00:40:41.044
Three tablespoons of water.
one of honey.

680
00:40:41.497 --> 00:40:42.627
Nothing more.

681
00:40:44.557 --> 00:40:47.297
If she knows something about
anything that's going on.

682
00:40:47.792 --> 00:40:50.497
I'm going to find it.

683
00:40:54.427 --> 00:40:55.928
Rise and shine. bitch!

684
00:40:55.958 --> 00:40:57.758
Breakfast.

685
00:41:35.286 --> 00:41:36.059
Michael?

686
00:41:36.099 --> 00:41:38.159
Hey. Michael!

687
00:41:40.029 --> 00:41:41.799
You all right?

688
00:41:41.829 --> 00:41:44.299
Yeah. I'm fine.

689
00:41:44.329 --> 00:41:46.729
All this security makes you wonder
what the Company's hiding.

690
00:41:47.230 --> 00:41:50.188
Only way to know for sure is
to find those five other cards.

691
00:41:50.660 --> 00:41:52.030
see for ourselves.

692
00:41:52.060 --> 00:41:54.130
Think we'll have enough time?

693
00:41:54.160 --> 00:41:55.560
Yeah.

694
00:41:55.600 --> 00:41:58.060
We'll. uh...

695
00:41:58.100 --> 00:41:59.760
We'll be fine.

695
